5,1,1,talk,Asuka,,"We need to be careful about the budget. A flat fee sounds simple, but hidden costs can create unfair burdens. Let's ensure we look into the actual financial breakdown and booking terms before deciding.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Shion,,"Budget is important, but efficiency is paramount. If the environment is poor, the training is wasted. We should prioritize the actual living conditions and the daily schedule to ensure everyone performs at their peak.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Minato,,I agree with both of you. I also think we should consider how much work it takes to organize everything. I don't want anyone to feel too overwhelmed by the preparations. What do you all think?,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. We need a destination that is sustainable both financially and logistically. To avoid any surprises, we should be very precise about the costs and the booking process this time.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Takumi,,"Costs and schedules are fine, but we can't forget the people. If we just pick a cheap place, we'll end up in the same cliques as last year. We need a spot that actually forces us to bond.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, bonding is important, but not at the cost of financial instability. We need a clear picture of the total expenditure. I suggest we divide the research to cover costs, logistics, and the facility's quality.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, a logical division is best. I'll focus on the actual environment and the daily flow. If we don't secure a place where people can actually rest, the entire camp becomes a failure regardless of the cost.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Minato,,That sounds like a good plan. I'm curious about how the booking process works and who has to do the work. I want to make sure the burden is shared and not too heavy for anyone.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Misaki,,I'll handle the financial side. I want to see the actual spending patterns and the terms for renting entire buildings to ensure we don't have any unexpected deficits this year.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, @Asuka, you guys are too focused on the money. If we don't fix the atmosphere, the camp is a waste. I'll look into how we can actually get people talking and mixing.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, atmosphere is a result of a well-managed environment. If the budget is unstable, stress will ruin the mood. I will look into the quoting terms for whole-building lets and the prefecture rate sheet for publicly run beds.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, your focus is narrow. I will look into the vacation timetable for the club's own hall and the attendance sheets for the away camps to analyze the actual flow and past failures.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Minato,,"I'll look into the lottery and application for public group bookings, and the canteen closure and last year's cooking duty. I want to see how much effort the booking and meal planning actually take.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Misaki,,I will look into the group transport in three years of receipts and the accounts from two clubs that went inland. I want to see the actual spending history to prevent any budget gaps.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Shion, @Minato, you're missing the point. I'll check what the seniors say about year-groups mixing and the membership list against first-train times to see who's actually coming and how to break those cliques.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Asuka,,"The division of tasks is clear. By analyzing the rate sheets and quoting terms, I can identify potential financial risks. Let's proceed with this research so we can make a logical, fair decision based on the data.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Shion,,Indeed. Data is the only way to avoid the inefficiency of last year. I'll analyze the schedules and attendance to ensure we don't repeat the same mistakes. I look forward to seeing if your financial focus yields anything useful.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Minato,,I hope we can find a place that is easy for everyone to manage. I'll do my best to find out about the workload so we can all enjoy the camp together.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Misaki,,I'll focus on the actual expenditures. It's better to be overly cautious now than to deal with a deficit later. I'll report back once I've analyzed the receipts and the other clubs' accounts.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Takumi,,"Fine. You guys handle the spreadsheets and the paperwork. I'll focus on the people. If we don't fix the divide between the year-groups, this camp is just a fancy trip for cliques. I'm on it.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
