35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My research reveals a significant risk with whole-building lets: deposits are non-refundable and based on a fixed headcount. If someone cancels late, the remaining members must cover the cost. We need a system to handle such liabilities.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, your financial risk is a symptom of a larger problem. My research shows a worrying trend of attrition; a fifth of members didn't even attend last time. If we book based on current numbers, we're inviting a deficit.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that public group bookings are a lot of work. The application is nine pages long and has to be redone if dates change. Also, cooking for ourselves takes hours every day. We should avoid that.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, I agree that we should avoid unnecessary burdens. My research shows that transport costs fluctuate wildly depending on distance. If we go too far, it could easily consume nearly 40% of our budget, risking another deficit.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Shion, that attrition is exactly why we need to change things. My research shows that bonding only happens when everyone sleeps in the same place. If we don't prioritize that, people will keep skipping.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, bonding is irrelevant if the cost becomes a burden for those who actually show up. @Shion, your data on attrition confirms my fear; a non-refundable deposit for a whole building is a dangerous gamble.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, exactly. It's a gamble with poor odds. Furthermore, using our own hall is out of the question; the schedule is too fragmented. We cannot expect peak performance if training is split between dawn and midnight.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Asuka, @Shion, if the booking process is that stressful and the deposits are risky, maybe we should look for something simpler? I'm worried that whoever handles the paperwork will be exhausted before the camp even starts.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, simplicity is key, but financial stability is non-negotiable. If we choose a distant location, the transport costs alone could bankrupt us. We must prioritize a destination that keeps travel expenses low and predictable.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, you're just talking about money again. If a third of the club can't even make it by 9 AM without a bed, we need a place where everyone stays together. That's how we stop the attrition @Shion mentioned.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, staying together is a goal, but not at the cost of financial instability. @Minato, @Misaki, given the risks of non-refundable deposits and high transport costs, a public facility with a flat per-student rate seems the most logical and fair option.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Minato"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, a flat rate is logical, but only if the facility is adequate. If we prioritize cost over quality, we risk another camp where half the group is exhausted. We need a place that guarantees proper rest.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Asuka, but public facilities have that nine-page application and the lottery. That sounds like a huge burden for the organizers. Can we find a place that is both affordable and easy to book?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, the administrative burden is a concern, but a budget deficit is a crisis. If we choose a private let to save time, we risk non-refundable losses. A local, public facility minimizes both transport costs and financial risk.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, @Asuka, you're both ignoring the human cost. If we just pick a ""safe"" public facility that's a pain to book, we're just checking boxes. We need a place that actually brings us together.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, the ""human cost"" includes the resentment members feel when they are forced to pay for someone else's cancellation. A public facility's per-person rate is the only way to ensure a fair and transparent distribution of costs.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, fairness is a baseline, not a goal. If we settle for a public facility just to avoid financial risk, we might end up with subpar sleeping conditions again. We must ensure the facility actually supports recovery.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,"I'm really worried about the organizers. If we pick a public facility, the lottery and that long application sound like a nightmare. Can't we find a place that's fair and comfortable, but doesn't require so much paperwork?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, I understand the paperwork is daunting, but it is a one-time effort. A budget gap, however, is a long-term burden on the club. We cannot afford to gamble with our funds again. Local and public is the safest path.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, @Asuka, you're so scared of a deficit that you're willing to let the club fall apart. If we don't prioritize a place where everyone stays together, the attrition will just get worse. That's the real crisis.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
