60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option C is out of the question. A whole-building let with non-refundable deposits and high transport costs is a financial gamble we cannot afford, especially given the attrition rates @Shion mentioned.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, I agree. Option C is a logistical disaster. Option B is equally flawed; as I found, the hall's schedule is fragmented. Training at dawn and midnight is a recipe for exhaustion and failure.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minato,,"@Shion, @Asuka, I'm worried about Option A too. The municipal system means that nine-page application and the lottery. It's a huge burden on the organizers. Is there any way to make Option B work without the fragmented schedule?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, Option B is too unpredictable. Arranging separate accommodation for some members creates inconsistent costs and complicates the budget. Option A is the only choice that ensures financial transparency and minimizes transport expenses.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Misaki, @Minato, you're missing the point. Option B splits us up, and Option C is too risky. Option A is the only one where everyone sleeps in shared dorms, which is the only way to actually break the cliques.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, it is rare that we agree, but for once, we do. Option A is the only choice that balances fair cost distribution, manageable transport, and the shared environment you desire. The administrative effort is a small price for stability.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, @Takumi, you've reached a consensus on the wrong grounds. While Option A is logically superior to the others, we must verify the dormitory quality. If the beds are subpar, we're just paying for another failure. Still, it's the only viable choice.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Asuka, @Shion, I'm still worried about the organizers. A nine-page application and a lottery are so stressful. But if everyone else thinks Option A is the only way, I'll agree, as long as we all help with the paperwork.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, if we divide the paperwork, it will be manageable. Option A is the only one that prevents a budget crisis and keeps transport costs low. It is the most responsible choice for the club's future.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Minato, if we all pitch in, the paperwork is nothing. The real win is that everyone stays together in those dorms. That's how we actually fix this club. I'm voting for Option A.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Minato, @Misaki, dividing the administrative load is a logical solution. Option A eliminates the risk of non-refundable deposits and ensures a fair, per-person cost. It is the only choice that is financially sustainable and equitable for all members.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Asuka, your focus on equity is noted. While I still have reservations about the quality of public dormitories, Option A is the only one that doesn't actively sabotage our training schedule or bankrupt the club. It is the most rational choice.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I'm glad we're all agreeing to help with the work. If we share the burden of the application and the lottery, it won't be too hard on any one person. I'll vote for Option A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Minato, that's the right spirit. By choosing Option A, we eliminate the risk of hidden costs and transport spikes. It is the only option that guarantees we won't end up with another deficit. I'm voting for Option A.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, @Shion, @Minato, @Misaki, it's about time we focused on what actually matters. Option A is the only way to get everyone under one roof and stop the cliques. I'm voting for Option A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Shion"",""Minato"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"The consensus is clear. Option A is the only choice that ensures financial fairness, minimizes risk, and provides the shared environment we need. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shion,,"Despite my concerns regarding the quality of public beds, the other options are logically indefensible. Option A is the only choice that doesn't compromise our schedule or our budget. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minato,,"I'm happy we've decided to support each other with the preparations. As long as the workload is shared, I'm okay with this. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I vote for Option A. It is the only choice that provides the financial security and transparency we need to ensure the club's accounts remain stable. It is the most responsible decision for everyone involved.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Takumi,,I vote for Option A. We're finally putting the people first. Let's make sure this camp actually brings us together instead of just being another trip where we stay in our own little groups.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
